From a7fd80d861c500b86d73815b405dea249f61cefd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:42:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Unlock 1Password with Windows Hello

An opt-in, root-only polkit agent registers only for the installed 1Password app of one desktop user, ported from Try Omarchy for macOS. When 1Password asks polkit for its unlock action, the agent asks the Windows Hello broker for a signed onepassword-unlock approval that reuses the sudo pairing, and answers polkit itself only after the broker verifies it. The operation and its 1password service are part of the signed client data, so a sudo approval cannot unlock 1Password or the other way round. A denied or unavailable Hello prompt, and every other 1Password or polkit request, goes to the standard PAM password dialog, which runs as the user.

sudo try-omarchy-windows-hello onepassword enable|disable turns the agent on or off; disabling Windows Hello also stops it. Revision 37 delivers the agent, dialog and unit to existing guests without enabling anything.
